# Security headers for every page (Cloudflare Pages reads this file; vercel.json has the same list).
# - No other site may show the app inside a frame (stops "clickjacking": a hidden Accept button under a fake page).
# - No plugins (<object>/<embed>), and the page's base address can't be changed by injected HTML.
# - The app never uses the camera, microphone or location, so nothing may ask for them.
# A full Content-Security-Policy (which scripts may run) is a later step: it needs testing with
# Supabase, Google sign-in, the PDF reader and the offline service worker first.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
